  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nFall weather with dry conditions is expected through Tuesday \nevening as high pressure affects the region. The exception may \nbe Sunday evening when a few light rain showers may briefly \ndrift in from the east across Northwest Pennsylvania. Temperatures\nwill be near to slightly below normal over the next several \ndays with highs in the upper 60s and lower 70s and lows in the \nupper 40s to mid 50s each day. By late Wednesday, weak low \npressure will move into the Midwest and Great Lakes region. \nForecast has trended drier on Wednesday with only isolated rain \nshowers, increasing a bit in coverage on Thursday and Friday. No\nthunderstorms are forecast.",
